						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: COLLISION DETECTION\n\nIn this example we use the Distance node to check whether the Circle is touching the Rectangles.\nTo achieve this we calculate the distance between the circle’s position (from the Perlin Generator nodes) and each rectangle (from the Grid Pattern node).\nIf any of the calculations results in less than 0.15, we turn the circle shape red, indicating a collision.\n\nThis is a very crude and rudimentary collision system, but could easily be expanded to do more complex actions based on the collisions."
					}
				},
